# Feature delivery

Before implementing or refactoring Ghostwriter domain, storage, API, editor, Canvas, UI, or
writer workflows, read and follow
`.cursor/skills/ghostwriter-feature-delivery/SKILL.md`.

That skill governs vertical checkpoints, parent-owned end-to-end acceptance, parallel research,
Composer/Grok delegation for most development, expensive Opus/GPT escalation, coherence review,
verification, and documentation. Trivial fixes (typos, one-liners) are exempt and do not need a
plan.

Do not start product code for a feature or epic until the active plan is truthful and the skill’s
Start + domain/design audit steps are underway. Keep analysis, planning, breakdown, synthesis, and
acceptance on the parent; delegate well-framed development and validation through
`delegate-composer` / `delegate-grok`, escalating to `escalate-opus` (creative) or `escalate-gpt`
(concrete) only with a recorded reason.
